TOKEN tinybird_read_public READ
TOKEN tinybird_read READ

DESCRIPTION >
Model health at two grains in one pass: one rollup row per model, plus one row
per execution route that served it.

Rows where `is_rollup` is 1 are the model total: what the caller experienced,
counting only the call that settled each request, so a rescued request counts as
the success it was. This matches what `model_health` reports. Rows where
`is_rollup` is 0 are a single execution route — the model's own primary, or a
fallback it fell through to — and count every call that route received,
including attempts that were retried elsewhere, so a primary that is quietly
failing cannot hide behind its rescues.

The two therefore do not add up, and the gap is the point: a model's routes
receive more calls than the model receives requests, by exactly the number of
attempts that were retried. `fallback_rescues` names how many of those retries
succeeded.

Both grains come from one GROUPING SETS pass, so a rollup and its routes always
describe the same traffic, and p50/p95 are computed correctly at each level
rather than derived from the other (percentiles cannot be combined after the
fact).

Column names match `model_health` so consumers reuse one health rule for both.
Time window is controlled by the `minutes` parameter (default 60).

NODE model_route_health_stats
SQL >
    %
    SELECT
        resolved_model_requested as model,
        event_type,
        model_used,
        -- Read through an aggregate rather than as a plain key: provider is a
        -- grouping key only at the route grain, so selecting it directly would
        -- leave every rollup row blank — and consumers read it to tell a
        -- community model from an official one.
        topK(1)(model_provider_used)[1] as provider,
        -- 1 on the model total, 0 on a single route. From GROUPING rather than
        -- an empty-string test, so it stays correct whatever model_used holds.
        GROUPING(model_used) as is_rollup,
        -- On a route: whether it serves as a fallback. On the rollup: whether
        -- any fallback fired for this model at all.
        max(fallback_used) as fallback_used,
        -- The two grains count different things on purpose.
        --
        -- A route counts every call it received, settled or retried elsewhere,
        -- because a primary that fails and gets rescued has to show that
        -- failure somewhere or it reads as healthy.
        --
        -- The rollup counts only the call that settled each request, so it is
        -- what the caller actually experienced — a rescued request succeeded,
        -- and says so. Counting attempts here would charge a model for a
        -- failure no user ever saw. This makes the rollup identical to
        -- `model_health`; the difference against its routes is the retried
        -- attempts, which `fallback_rescues` accounts for.
        if(GROUPING(model_used) = 1, countIf(is_final), count()) as total_requests,
        if(
            GROUPING(model_used) = 1,
            countIf(is_final AND response_status >= 200 AND response_status < 300),
            countIf(response_status >= 200 AND response_status < 300)
        ) as status_2xx,
        if(
            GROUPING(model_used) = 1,
            countIf(is_final AND response_status >= 400 AND response_status < 500),
            countIf(response_status >= 400 AND response_status < 500)
        ) as errors_4xx,
        if(
            GROUPING(model_used) = 1,
            countIf(is_final AND response_status >= 500),
            countIf(response_status >= 500)
        ) as errors_5xx,
        -- How many of these calls were the one the caller actually received.
        -- Summed over a model's routes this equals its request count, which is
        -- what `model_health` reports.
        countIf(is_final) as served,
        countIf(
            -- Qualified: the SELECT aliases `fallback_used` to max(fallback_used)
            -- above, and an unqualified reference here would resolve to that
            -- aggregate, which ClickHouse rejects as a nested aggregate.
            is_final AND generation_event_v2.fallback_used
            AND response_status >= 200 AND response_status < 300
        ) as fallback_rescues,
        -- Non-final 503s retried elsewhere: capacity pressure, not a
        -- caller-visible failure.
        countIf(NOT is_final AND response_status = 503) as retried_503s,
        maxIf(start_time, response_status >= 500) as last_error_at,
        -- Route latency excludes earlier attempts. Historical rows without
        -- attempt timing are omitted instead of assigning request latency.
        round(if(
            GROUPING(model_used) = 1,
            quantileIf(0.5)(response_time, response_status >= 200 AND response_status < 300),
            quantileIf(0.5)(attempt_response_time, response_status >= 200 AND response_status < 300)
        ), 0) as latency_p50_ms,
        round(if(
            GROUPING(model_used) = 1,
            quantileIf(0.95)(response_time, response_status >= 200 AND response_status < 300),
            quantileIf(0.95)(attempt_response_time, response_status >= 200 AND response_status < 300)
        ), 0) as latency_p95_ms,
        round(if(
            GROUPING(model_used) = 1,
            avgIf(response_time, response_status >= 200 AND response_status < 300),
            avgIf(attempt_response_time, response_status >= 200 AND response_status < 300)
        ), 0) as avg_latency_ms,
        max(start_time) as last_request_at,
        -- Completion tokens per second of full request duration, same
        -- definition as model_health. Computed per group, so the rollup is the
        -- true combined rate rather than an average of its routes' rates.
        if(
            sumIf(
                response_time,
                response_status >= 200 AND response_status < 300
                AND (token_count_completion_text > 0 OR token_count_completion_reasoning > 0)
                AND response_time > 0
            ) > 0,
            round(
                sumIf(
                    toUInt64(token_count_completion_text) + toUInt64(token_count_completion_reasoning),
                    response_status >= 200 AND response_status < 300
                    AND (token_count_completion_text > 0 OR token_count_completion_reasoning > 0)
                    AND response_time > 0
                )
                / (
                    sumIf(
                        response_time,
                        response_status >= 200 AND response_status < 300
                        AND (token_count_completion_text > 0 OR token_count_completion_reasoning > 0)
                        AND response_time > 0
                    ) / 1000
                ),
                1
            ),
            NULL
        ) as tokens_per_second
    FROM generation_event_v2
    WHERE start_time >= now() - interval {{Int32(minutes, 60)}} minute
    -- provider is deliberately not a key: a route id already determines it, and
    -- keying on it would make it unaggregatable and leave rollup rows blank.
    GROUP BY GROUPING SETS (
        (model, event_type, model_used),
        (model, event_type)
    )
    ORDER BY model, event_type, is_rollup DESC, total_requests DESC

TYPE endpoint
